LAMMPS (22 Jul 2025 - Update 1)
# Created by Siamak Attarian (sattarian@wisc.edu, siamak.attarian@gmail.com)
# For more information, see below article:
# "S.Attarian, D.Morgan, I.Szlufarska, Thermophysical properties of FLiBe using moment tensor potentials, Journal of Molecular Liquids, 2022"
# This tempelate file is used to calculate the density, diffusivity, thermal expansion coefficient,
# radial distribution function, specific heat capacity and bulk modulus of FLiBe.
# The output files are post processed to obtain the mentioned properties.
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#----------------------------- General setting -------------------------------
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
clear
units metal
dimension 3
boundary p p p
atom_style atomic

#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#---------------------------- Importing atoms --------------------------------
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
read_data FLiBe_800K.data
Reading data file ...
  orthogonal box = (-0.079542 -0.078601 9.179485) to (13.167224 13.224185 15.414564)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
  reading atoms ...
  98 atoms
  read_data CPU = 0.000 seconds

#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#-------------------- Grouping for MSD calculations---------------------------
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
group Lithium type 1
28 atoms in group Lithium
group Berylium type 2
14 atoms in group Berylium
group Fluorine type 3
56 atoms in group Fluorine

#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#------------------------- Interatomic Potential -----------------------------
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
pair_style mlip mlip.ini
ERROR: Unrecognized pair style 'mlip' (../force.cpp:275)
Last input line: pair_style mlip mlip.ini
